<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania's Vilniaus Bank H1 net profit up.</title>
<headline>Lithuania's Vilniaus Bank H1 net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1997.</p>
<p>			    (million litas unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit	21.7		vs	11.7</p>
<p> Assets	    1.11 billion    vs	914.7</p>
<p> Total deposits  763		 vs	589.6</p>
<p> Loans	     493.5	     vs	356.3</p>
<p>Note: All figures except for net profit compared to end of 1996. Net profit compared to first half 1996.</p>
<p>The bank said its average return on equity was 16.95 percent, and its average return on assets was 2.19 percentage points. Its capital adequacy ratio as of June 30 was 21.3 percent.</p>
<p>Vilniaus Bank is Lithuania's leading privately owned commercial bank and is included on the official list of the Vilnius stock exchange.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
</text>
